{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788917823,"nonce":"VZOdYZPTimN+meJKGrS+6rD5jYE=","title":"A bundling verb must default to the narrowest scope and say what else it wrote","message":"THEME T8, filed 2026-09-08 from the openrun-20260902 audit, where it was the one\nCONFIRMED theme still marked UNFILED. It is the second link in the agent's own causal\nchain for the wipe.\n\nWHY IT WAS NOT FILED BEFORE. It is a direct consequence of a CLOSED issue rather than\na regression. b1b3060 made `posture` write three settings together on purpose, and\nthat reasoning is sound. What nothing says is that a verb which bundles must also\ndefault to the narrowest SCOPE, and must report the levers it wrote where the caller\ncannot filter them away.\n\nTHE RUN'S EVIDENCE, all confirmed from the journal's own `levers` arrays:\n\n- `posture` with no `pawns` unbound all seven colonists. The agent needed to free ONE\n  rescuer to reach the downed Dilly, issued the call with no pawn filter, and never\n  re-bound anyone. When the fatal raid landed about 270,000 ticks later, all seven\n  were scattered 40 to 70 cells outside the walls. The scoped form (--pawns [53017])\n  existed and the agent used it correctly twenty minutes later in the same slice.\n  (F-S12-10)\n- `posture {area:null}` also flipped `seek` ON for Ellis, Shooting 0, 250 cells from\n  base. Caught only because the agent happened to read the `after` block. (F-S02-7)\n- `posture --area lockdown` flipped `will_seek` true for John and Anon: \"that would\n  send two unarmoured men out to hunt a scyther\". (F-S10-22)\n- `posture {seek:true}` sent pawns hunting map-wide. Tony walked about 130 cells to\n  melee shamblers; John was downed doing the same, which began the infection chain\n  that killed him. The agent's own words: \"seek: true was overreach\". (F-S08-13,\n  F-S09-1, F-S09-7)\n- `attack` with no `mode` defaults to `auto` and routed a Melee-3 pawn with a revolver\n  into melee with a scyther. (F-S10-23)\n- `auto_arm` re-picks weapons and scored a poor autopistol over a good bolt-action,\n  silently reverting a deliberate equip. (F-S11-8)\n\nWHY IT IS BEING FILED NOW, AND WHY IT IS NOT COVERED BY THE COCKPIT. A blind review of\nthe cockpit's honesty defences on 2026-09-08 (RUNS/openrun-20260902/audit/ROUNDS.md)\nreturned this as the seventh defence the other six leave open. Every one of those six\nREPORTS a mistake after it happened; this one stops the write. It also cuts against\nthe chore defence, which argues the mod should act unasked, so the two are stated\ntogether deliberately: a chore may act unasked, a VERB may not write a lever its\ncaller did not name.\n\nIt is not covered by the screen. A screen shows an unbound colonist after the call\nthat unbound them, and this run proves that is too late: the agent read the `after`\nblock twice and caught two of these, and missed the one that mattered.\n\nACCEPTANCE:\n\n- Every verb that writes more than one lever names, in DESIGN.md, the levers it writes\n  and its default scope. A verb with no explicit scope argument defaults to the\n  narrowest scope it can act on, never to \"all\".\n- `posture` with no `pawns` is refused, not widened. This is already the ruling in\n  COCKPIT.md's §Where it lives generalisation of 7382bdd; this issue is where it lands\n  in the mod.\n- Every bundling verb's result carries the levers it actually wrote, and the cockpit\n  screen prints \"you also changed X\" for any lever written that the caller did not\n  name. The journal already records the `levers` array, so the fact exists; what is\n  missing is the refusal and the prominence.\n- A regression fixture covers the three shapes this run hit: an omitted scope\n  argument, an omitted mode argument that defaults to a mutating value, and a bundled\n  lever the caller did not pass.\n- The audit's theme T8 can be moved from UNFILED to COVERED by this id.\n\nNOT IN SCOPE: re-opening b1b3060. The three-lever bundle stays; only its scope\ndefault and its reporting change.","files":null}]}